{"reference":"Romans 2","book":"Romans","chapter":2,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Questions About Judgment and Conscience","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter’s language about Gentiles acting “by nature” and conscience bearing witness should not be read as modern biological or scientific language. Conscience is portrayed as an inner witness that may accuse or defend, not as an infallible and culture-free moral guide. Interpreters also disagree whether the Gentiles in verses 14–16 are actual Gentiles, Gentile Christ-followers, a hypothetical case, or a rhetorical figure; the passage itself does not settle the question.","verse_refs":["Romans 2:13-29","Romans 2:14","Romans 2:14-16","Romans 2:6-29"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_romans_002_8f349be9e4ca560355e3498b","reader_path_romans_002_7b80741f89bb344b8becc275"],"confidence":"low","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"why_it_matters","title":"Impartial Judgment and Identity","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"Romans 2 addresses both Jew and Greek under impartial judgment, then contrasts outward circumcision with circumcision of the heart. These categories should not be collapsed into a claim that Jewish identity is fraudulent or obsolete, nor should Gentile inclusion be turned into collective Jewish blame or replacement ownership. The chapter’s critique is directed at transgression and self-contradiction, not at making one people the disposable example of another’s innocence.","verse_refs":["Romans 2:1-16","Romans 2:17-29","Romans 2:25-29"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_romans_002_760067db39e524a76a504d27"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"A Note on Approval","blocks":[{"id":"block_3","text":"No automated validation, retrieval score, confessional popularity, or manuscript count by itself constitutes human approval of a Romans record.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_romans_002_5c66bc488486de3abd2b1137"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"inference"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}